---
import ContentLayout from '../../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import { enemies } from '../../data/game.js';

const slug = (t) => t.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z]+/g, '-');
---
<ContentLayout
  title="ARC Enemy Database"
  description="Every ARC machine in ARC Raiders with weak points, stagger windows, grenade counters and loot drops — from Ticks to the Queen."
  eyebrow="ARC Enemies"
  heading="Every machine, and how to break it"
  lede="ARC armor follows a consistent colour system. Learning to read it is the difference between a twenty-round kill and burning half your ammo on plating."
>
  <h2>Read the armor before you shoot</h2>
  <p>
    ARC machines use three armor states, and they are visible. White parts are
    unarmored and take full damage from any weapon — this is your default aim
    point when nothing better is exposed. Grey parts are armored and soak damage.
    Yellow marks a genuine weak point, and hitting one is worth repositioning
    for.
  </p>
  <div class="callout">
    <p>
      <strong>Sticky grenades matter.</strong> Several weak points — the Bastion's
      back panel in particular — can only be reached reliably with a grenade that
      sticks. Bouncing grenades slide off. Carry Snap Hooks or Triggers if you
      expect heavy ARC.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Full enemy database</h2>
  <div class="enemy-list">
    {enemies.map(e => (
      <article class="hud-card enemy-card">
        <span class={`tag threat threat-${slug(e.threat)}`}>Threat: {e.threat}</span>
        <h3>{e.name}</h3>
        <p class="weak"><strong>Weak point:</strong> {e.weakPoint}</p>
        <p>{e.strategy}</p>
        {e.loot && <p class="loot"><strong>Notable drops:</strong> {e.loot}</p>}
      </article>
    ))}
  </div>

  <h2>Bosses are not solo content</h2>
  <p>
    The Matriarch and the Queen are built for coordinated teams with full heavy
    loadouts and grenade stocks. Solo kills exist and get posted, but they are
    endurance runs rather than a reasonable farming strategy. If you want boss
    loot consistently, bring a trio, bring Wolfpacks, and farm on
    <a href="/maps/dam-battlegrounds"> Dam Battlegrounds</a>.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .enemy-list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 20px; margin-top: 24px; }
  .enemy-card p { font-size: 0.93rem; }
  .enemy-card .weak { margin-bottom: 10px; }
  .enemy-card .weak strong, .enemy-card .loot strong { color: var(--color-text); }
  .enemy-card .loot { margin-bottom: 0; font-size: 0.86rem; }
  .enemy-card .tag { border-bottom-color: currentColor; }
  @media (max-width: 800px) { .enemy-list { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
